{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>Or has any god [Elohim] tried.</b> Some say it is in profane language, and far be it, far be it — rather it is sacred language:" "<b>Has tried.</b> In the manner of human beings, so that the listeners will understand:" "<b>By trials.</b> A general term, or its meaning is 'by trials' that were in signs, like 'and he performed the signs before the people' [Exodus 4:30]:" "<b>And by wonders.</b> The ten plagues, as it is written, 'and Moses and Aaron performed' [Exodus 7:20]:" "<b>And by war.</b> It is possible this refers to the killing of the firstborn and judgments upon the gods of Egypt:" "<b>And by a mighty hand.</b> That Israel went out with a high hand and an outstretched arm, corresponding to the pillar of fire and cloud:" "<b>And by great terrors.</b> The drowning of Pharaoh and his army, along with the splitting of the sea for Israel:" "<b>In Egypt.</b> Upon the people of Egypt:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:22:21.342386728Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}